Accepted by the main session, 2026-08-10.

NewFetcher and FetchAt measure 0% in the unit-coverage run because their
only honest exercise needs a real broker, and that exercise exists on
this branch: fetch/fetcher_integration_test.go runs the roadmap's
verification criteria (a) round-trip byte-identical, (b) superseded
after real compaction, (c) evicted by retention, behind -tags
integration, invisible to the unit coverage measurement.

The suite was executed by the main session, uncached, against a fresh
dev-loop broker on this branch:
  just redpanda-down && just redpanda-up
  go test -tags integration -count=1 -race ./fetch/
  -> ok github.com/sonirico/rpkv/fetch 4.719s (exit 0)

Unit-mocking *kgo.Client would test the mock and contradict the
black-box contract-test discipline (repo CLAUDE.md, ADR-002).
verifyFetch, the unit-testable classification logic, is at 100%.
